  "abstract": "NetworkManager is a system network service that manages network devices and connections, attempting to keep active network connectivity when available. Its capabilities include managing Ethernet, wireless, mobile broadband (WWAN), and PPPoE devices, as well as providing VPN integration with a variety of different VPN services.\n\nBug Fix(es):\n\n* Better dispatch way for DNS changes (JIRA:RHEL-14885)\n\n* [NMCI] ovs_mtu crashing  (JIRA:RHEL-17838)\n\n* Reapply of device network update DNS changes retrieved from DHCPv4 to /etc/resolv.conf (JIRA:RHEL-20599)\n\n* [FJ8.7 Bug]: Suppress NetworkManager's harmless warning when IPv6 is disabled at kernel level (JIRA:RHEL-24967)",
